From 2567682f131aae6e7504beea6e7c96eab18e4779 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:07:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/54] hw/display/pvg: Metal executor v0 on Vulkan

Executes render segments of ExecIndirect2 command buffers on the host GPU:
render passes as dynamic rendering, pipelines from the serialized
descriptor + air2spv-translated functions, buffers via a host-visible
arena with device addresses, textures uploaded from their linear guest
copies, render targets stored back to guest memory (so presented
backings show the result). Fence per submit; the first failed or timed
out submit disables the executor (the host GPU drives the host desktop).
Bounds checks on buffer offsets and index ranges. exec=, exec-dry-run=
properties; dump-dir also saves translated metallibs.

Translator: per-stage push-constant base, typed splat constants, float to
bool conversions, 32-bit sampled image types with half results, narrow
vertex_id parameters, per-binding texture view kinds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
